Revision history for Class-Abstract

0.03	Thu Nov  5 09:51:37 AM EST 2026
	[ Incompatible Changes ]
	- $config{harness_bypass} now defaults to 0: enforcement is no longer
	  switched off when HARNESS_ACTIVE is set, so test suites catch
	  accidental instantiation of abstract classes.  Set it back to 1, or
	  use local $Class::Abstract::BYPASS = 1, to restore the old behaviour.
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- Bump minimum Test::Mockingbird, fixes RT#178677
	- is_abstract(), new() and check_abstract() no longer create the
	  package they are asked about in the symbol table
	- Class::Abstract->is_abstract($obj) now checks the object's class
	  (it used to check the stringified reference and always return 0)
	- is_abstract() croaks on an unblessed reference, as new() does
	- Objects blessed into package '0' are accepted as invocants
	- undef elements in @ISA no longer cause warnings
	[ Enhancements ]
	- check_abstract()'s unblessed-reference message names the reftype
	- POD rewritten: per-routine examples, API specifications, messages
	  and Z specifications; LIMITATIONS section
	[ Tests ]
	- New t/locales.t; regression tests for all of the above

0.02	Thu Jun 11 10:07:13 EDT 2026
	[ Bug Fixes ]
	- Added Test::Mockingbird prereq to testing

0.01	Thu Jun 11 08:33:08 EDT 2026
        First release
